---
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Airworthy Supply privacy policy for website, RFQ form submissions, and notifications."
>
  <section class="mt-12">
    <SectionHeader
      kicker="Privacy"
      headingTag="h1"
      title="Privacy and data handling policy"
      description="This page summarizes how Airworthy Supply handles website and RFQ submission data."
    />

    <div
      class="surface-panel space-y-6 p-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted sm:p-8 sm:text-base"
    >
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-ink">Information collected</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We collect contact and request data that you submit through the RFQ
          form, including company name, contact person, email, phone, parts
          requested, destination, cert requirement, needed-by details, and
          notes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-ink">
          Form provider and notifications
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          RFQ intake is handled through Tally form embeds. Submission
          notifications may be sent to the Airworthy Supply team via Cloudflare
          Pages Functions and MailChannels Email API.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-ink">How data is used</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Data is used to evaluate sourcing requests, communicate quotes, verify
          transaction integrity, and support service operations. We do not sell
          submitted data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-ink">Retention and access</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We keep submission records as needed for commercial handling,
          compliance review, and auditability. Contact us to request updates or
          deletion where legally and operationally feasible.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
